this is an incident that unfolded just  after seven o'clock in this park in the  center of reading we understand that  multiple people were stabbed the  information that we are now receiving as  three people have died from their  injuries a number of other people are  being treated in hospital for their  injuries ear ambulance and other  emergency responders were very quickly  on scene and tending to those who'd been  stabbed but it's clear in addition to  those who are believed to have died a  number of the other people who were  injured have been quite seriously  injured this evening our source has told  me that authorities are working under  the assumption that this incident is  terror related we are expecting some  kind of statement from the police a more  substantial statement from the police  probably within the next hour or so of  course as I say it unfolded at 7:00  o'clock this evening police have been  trying to piece together the exact  circumstances around what is now  believed had been a terrorist incident  we know that one man has been arrested  now the press association is reporting  that this man was a libyan national we  have not been able to confirm that line  for ourselves but that is being reported  by the Press Association at this hour we  have been able to confirm through our  own sources that three people are  believed to have died and as I say that  significant development that it is being  treated as a terrorist incident now of  course that has all kinds of  implications for the authorities in  terms of how they deal with this  incident now because any terrorist  related incident has a potential to have  a wider threat alongside it so as a  matter of urgency the investigators from  the southeast terrorism unit along with  those of course at Scotland Yard will be  delving into this man's background  trying to  find out who exactly he is whether he  was known to the police and security  services sadly of course we have seen  with other terrorist attacks that the  majority of those who carry out  terrorist attacks are known to the  authorities because these incidents  rarely happen in isolation in the sense  that someone is often on a journey into  extremism heading down towards violent  extremism and they will often come  across the radar of the police and the  security services we don't know at this  stage whether this man who is in custody  was known to police and security  services but even if he was they have a  judgment call to make to determine  whether anyone should be worthy of a  full investigation about the potential  actions but the the urgent priority  actually will be to determine whether  there are other individuals out there  who know this man who associate with  this man who may have had knowledge of  what the person that carried out the  stabbing attacks was planning whether  there is any wider threat in terms of  the potential for other attacks we know  of course a terrorist threat level at  the moment has been reduced to  substantial it was reduced to  substantial last year having been at  severe for a number of years severe of  course means that a terrorist attack is  highly likely it was at severe in 2017  when we had those five terrorist attacks  in the space of just one year but the  Joint Terrorism analysis Center who look  at the the threat picture that's out  there they involve of course members of  the security services and other security  officials determined that it should be  reduced to substantial still meaning  that an attack is likely but not highly  likely as the severe definition  determined so that of course will be  reviewed as well in the coming hours if  they get information of the potential of  other others out there or potential for  other attacks then of course the threat  level would be  increased but there is no indication  that that is on the cards at this stage  were still in the very early stages  offer police and counterterrorism  investigation as I said we are hoping  within the hour to hear a bit more from  Thames Valley Police perhaps from  counterterrorism policing as well about  the ongoing investigation the Press  Association reporting that the man in  custody is a Libyan national and we are  reporting of course that they are  treating this as a terrorist incident  one other point of clarification that's  worth getting out there Thames Valley  Police have tweeted this evening to say  that these multiple reports on social  media suggesting that there is some link  to black lives matter are erroneous  there was a black lives matter protest  that took place in that area earlier  today as there has been in previous  weekends as well but they say there's  absolutely no length that they can see  to the black lives matter protests are  worth getting that out there and  certainly with the confirmation that  this is being treated at this stage they  believe as a terrorist incident it would  seem to back up what the police are  suggesting there as well the injured  have been taken to area hospitals we  know that the Royal Berkshire Hospital  in Redding has received a number of  casualties at least two of those  seriously injured are in resuscitation  resource at the moment in the accident  and emergency department being treated  by those doctors at the scene so some  significant injuries in addition to the  three people who died you can see in  that image that we're showing you now  two ear ambulances among those that  responded to the scene to this park in  Redding to pick up the most seriously  injured in addition to these air  ambulances there were paramedic and  senior paramedic officers that attended  the scene as well and in the early  minutes after this incident armed police  were involved as well because of course  we had a suspect at large at that time  we understand that that suspect was  arrested nearby now there are other  images circulating of an armed operation  at a block of flats on the edges of this  park we haven't had it officially  confirmed that that is linked to the man  you can see the images there of the  block of flats but certainly the  suggestion from journalists down there  the scene in reading is that the arrest  which involved on police at this block  of flats in Redding is linked to the  incident and is linked to the man who is  now in custody who is a see the press  association is reporting is a libyan  national the Home Secretary of course of  the Prime Minister and others being kept  up to speed with what is happening Priti  Patel said earlier this evening that she  was very concerned at the reports coming  out similar sentiment from the prime  minister who has issued his thoughts  with those who have been caught up in  this attack and thoughts with the police  and first responders who have been  dealing with what is clearly a very  troubling traumatic incident in this  March return
 

